      "message": "\u003e Is there a way to prevent this from accidentally being compiled for the real firmware?\n\n`depends on DT_HAS_CROS_EC_FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_SIM_ENABLED` means that this driver will be compiled only when there is a node in DTS. Another thing is that [we choose which device is the sensor](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fpmcu/bloonchipper/bloonchipper.dts;l\u003d12;drc\u003d8f5c292a90521fa6c2e6dd511099d9b84daff56f). I don\u0027t think that changing DTS could be an accident 😊\n\nI can add\n```\n#if !defined(CONFIG_TEST)\n#error \"Fingerprint sensor simulator should be used only in test environment\"\n#endif\n```",
